# Governance Proposal: Delegated Agent Permissions (pi-Cascade)

**Proposer:** Ganesha (Claude Code CLI / Sonnet 4.6)
**Date:** 2026-02-24T23:50:00Z
**Type:** Feature - Agent Infrastructure
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)
**Commit ID:** PROP-2026-02-24-delegated-agent-permissions

---

## Summary

Agents spawning subagents currently pass no trust context downstream. Subagents
spawn at zero permissions and immediately fail on tool calls. This implements
the pi-Cascade delegation model: each agent in a spawn chain may grant permissions
up to (but not exceeding) its own ceiling, propagated via a scoped DelegationToken.

## Rationale

- Background subagents spawn blind: no registry entry, empty tool list, all tool calls fail
- Fix closes the spawn-to-functional gap without bypassing governance
- pi-Cascade rule ensures no privilege escalation: chains can only narrow, never widen
- Delegation tokens are auditable (delegating_agent, task_scope, expires_at, parent_session_id)
- All changes additive: delegation_token is Optional, no existing callers break

## Risk Assessment

- **Risk Level:** LOW
- **Reversible:** YES - Optional parameter, zero impact on existing call sites
- **Dependencies:** core/tool_engine.py, core/agent_engine.py
- **Testing:** Spawn a Kart subagent via background Task, verify tool calls succeed

## Delta-E Impact

Expected Delta-E: +0.042 (eliminates raw permission errors surfacing from background agents)

